# Tailwind CSS v4

- Use Tailwind v4 syntax; do not use deprecated v3 utilities.
- Import Tailwind with `@import "tailwindcss"` in CSS, not `@tailwind base/components/utilities`.
- Configure theme in CSS with `@theme` when extending; avoid legacy `tailwind.config.js` unless the project already uses it.
- Use `gap-*` for spacing in flex/grid layouts; support `dark:` when the app already uses dark mode.
- Match existing Tailwind patterns in sibling files before inventing new class combinations.

## Boundaries

- Do not add Tailwind to projects that use plain CSS only (see `project.mdc` or SPA rules).
- Tailwind rules apply to `resources/**` in Laravel apps, not necessarily to separate Vue SPA repos.
